add('TK-01','Critical','Intermittent Tk SIGSEGV remains an open release-stability gate','docs/v0.9.72/LIC_Import_Test_Results.md:11-37; tests/test_xsection.py:1866-1920','Tk update during Cross Section reopen','The supplied current release report records an exit139 fault in Tk8.6 during the settings reopen test. No native root cause has been established. A passing later run does not close the fault.','Use the original full order/runtime and a native debugger. This audit independently runs the complete available source suite once under gdb; see final Audit_Evidence for its actual outcome.','Long GUI sessions complete without native fault; closure rests on a captured/understood reproducer, not selected green reruns.','Supplied v0.9.72 evidence: Tk8.6 run1 crashed, then Tk9 and Tk8.6 passed. Those are author-supplied results, separate from this audit run. The original cause remains unresolved.','full-serial/pytest-native.log; docs/v0.9.72/LIC_Import_Test_Results.md; prior focused Tk audit','Capture the native fault and correct the demonstrated owner/thread lifecycle path. Preserve traces and test order. Do not label the issue fixed merely because this audit run or a targeted run passes.','Windows impact and frozen executable behavior are unverified; do not presume a Linux Tcl panic is the same SIGSEGV.','High for supplied open crash; Low for exact root cause','Supplied native crash evidence; original root cause unresolved')
add('TK-02','High','Destroyed Geo roots remain strongly owned by traces and selection subscriptions','geoworkbench/main_window.py:174,383,2671-2681; geoworkbench/common.py:97-126; ogcore/well_selection.py:41-56','Geo destruction; DepthEditTracker','Raw destroy bypasses normal listener cleanup and variable trace callbacks retain the owner graph. Normal close removes the listener but does not prove every trace graph is released.','Run probes/ownership_probe.py on v0.9.72: ten raw root destruction cycles, main-thread GC, then separate diagnostic listener/search/all-owner-trace removal controls.','Disposed owners are releasable on their owner thread; fixtures do not carry obsolete roots into unrelated tests.','Ten destroyed roots/listeners remain; removing listeners or search traces alone is insufficient; removing the remaining210 variable traces releases all ten. Diagnostic cleanup changes only disposable probe objects.','retention/ownership_probe.py.log','Own each trace/subscription token and provide idempotent disposal for supported destruction paths. Do not blanket-delete all variable traces in production.','Normal close versus raw destroy, worker lifetime and fixture teardown; no proof this causes original SIGSEGV or leaks client processes after they exit.','High for retention; Low for SIGSEGV causality','Confirmed retention on exercised path; possible native-crash contributor')
add('TK-03','High','Petro search trace retains destroyed application roots','petroworkbench/app.py:387-395,460-488','API search trace; Petro destruction','The variable trace retains a bound owner method after raw destruction.','Run probes/petro_retention.py: ten raw destroy/GC cycles and diagnostic owner trace cleanup.','No linear retention of disposed root graphs across repeated GUI lifecycle tests.','Ten roots retained; removing ten trace commands releases all ten (16320 objects collected).','retention/petro_retention.py.log','Retain/remove the search trace token in owner disposal and exercise all termination paths.','Do not lose search/filter state or infer Windows customer memory leakage from a raw-destroy test alone.','High for retention; Low for SIGSEGV causality','Confirmed retention on exercised path; possible contributor')
add('TK-04','High','Wrong-thread finalization remains a demonstrated native Tcl failure class','CPython _tkinter Tkapp_Dealloc; Tcl_AsyncDelete; tests/conftest.py:116-133','Finalization of cyclic Tk-owning graphs','The earlier isolated same-runtime probe proves a destroyed root cycle collected on a worker can panic Tcl without Workbench or Matplotlib. Existing main-thread fixture collection cannot collect graphs still strongly rooted by traces.','Use the prior focused audit minimal_gc.py in disposable subprocesses; compare owner-thread collection with deliberate worker collection/allocation. This is a controlled negative test, not the original application crash.','Application owners are deterministically disposed on their owning thread; workers hold plain data.','Prior native stacks: Tk8.6.16 SIGABRT through Tcl_AsyncDelete/Tkapp_Dealloc; Tk9.0.4 SIGILL panic trap. Main controls pass. Neither signal is the reported SIGSEGV139.','prior focused Tk native traces; runtime-Tk86.json; runtime-Tk9.json','Release Tk-containing graphs deterministically on their owner thread; keep the existing fixture guard as mitigation, not closure.','No global GC disabling; do not substitute this controlled panic for original SIGSEGV reproduction. The v0.9.72 application trigger remains unproved.','High for controlled native failure; Low for link to SIGSEGV','Confirmed root cause of controlled panic only; original link unresolved')
add('TK-05','Medium','Geo destruction leaves startup and poll timers naming deleted Tcl commands','geoworkbench/main_window.py:171-175,2671-2681','startup_project; _poll_requests','Owner timers are not explicitly cancelled before destruction deletes their callback commands.','Run probes/timer_probe.py: destroy a disposable Geo root, then inspect Tcl after info and info commands directly.','No queued callbacks reference deleted owner commands after disposal.','Two timers remain, startup_project and _poll_requests; both script_command_exists flags are false. No native fault is inferred.','timer-probe.log','Store/cancel owner job IDs before command destruction and prevent rescheduling after disposal.','Startup delay, polling, unexpected close and parent/child cancellation ordering.','High for stale callbacks; Low for native causality','Confirmed stale callback state; possible contributor')
add('TK-06','Medium','Repeated-root fixtures amplify lifecycle state left by earlier modules','tests/test_xsection.py:977-1010,1717-1755,2202-2221; tests/conftest.py:92-133','WindowTests; PunchListWindowTests; GeoCrossSectionTests','Tests repeatedly create roots, pump update and use raw destruction; strong graphs can outlive their fixture despite owner-thread GC. This differs from a desktop process ending on close.','Compare the recorded fresh, ordered and long-process runs in the focused audit and this full serial run; inspect the direct teardown calls and current retention controls.','Fixtures have explicit owner/worker/callback cleanup and serial stress remains meaningful.','Current ten-cycle probes confirm retained roots. Test-order/finalization timing is a supported amplification hypothesis; no proof identifies this as the original SIGSEGV trigger.','retention logs; full-serial log; prior focused audit A-D logs','Correct owner cleanup, assert weak-reference/callback baselines and keep a long serial stress job; subprocess isolation can contain independent groups but cannot prove a product fix.','Do not hide failures by weakening tests or replacing serial qualification with only isolated runs.','Medium','Strongly supported amplification hypothesis')
add('TK-07','Medium','Embedded figure ownership still needs sequence-level qualification','xsection/window.py:96-164,1649-1670; Matplotlib _backend_tk.py','Embedded canvas lifecycle; raster idle processing','Embedded figures are not all tracked by pyplot Gcf. Long GUI processes can retain graphs through owners, and nested idle pumping changes finalization timing. No native Matplotlib fault was proved.','Use actual Figure/canvas weak references and owner cleanup checks under the full GUI sequence, not only pyplot.close/Gcf.','Owner/canvas/job counts return to defined baselines after close and owner-thread collection.','Earlier focused audit:800 isolated section cycles ended with zero retained sections/Figures after GC; mixed sequence retained many graphs. Current full-run memory is recorded separately; it is not a new figure-count measurement.','prior focused Tk lifecycle/sequence evidence; full-serial resource logs; section-job-results.json','Trace retained owners before changing canvas integration; qualify idle draw, toolbar, bindings and close during raster preparation on both toolkit versions.','Keep renderers independent; high-water RSS alone is not proof of a leak, and no evidence supports blaming a library by name alone.','Medium for ownership risk; Low for SIGSEGV cause','Possible contributing factor; not a confirmed native library defect')
